Authorization: Bearer {{ipAuth.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: text/plain

{
  "address": "192.168.99.99"
}

# ========================================
# 📝 IP DELETION BLOCKING TEST NOTES
# ========================================
#
# NEW FEATURE: IP Deletion Blocking
# ✅ Block deletion of IP addresses assigned to servers
# ✅ Block deletion of IP addresses assigned to devices
# ✅ Return 409 Conflict with descriptive error message
# ✅ Allow deletion of unassigned IP addresses
# ✅ Proper error handling (404 for not found, 409 for conflict)
#
# ERROR RESPONSES:
# ✅ 409 - "Cannot delete IP address: it is assigned to server 'Server Name'"
# ✅ 409 - "Cannot delete IP address: it is assigned to device 'Device Name'"
# ✅ 409 - "Cannot delete IP address: it is assigned to server 'Server Name' and device 'Device Name'"
# ✅ 404 - "IP address not found"
# ✅ 204 - No Content (successful deletion)
#
# IMPLEMENTATION DETAILS:
# ✅ Check server_id and device_id columns in ip_addresses table
# ✅ Query related server and device names for error messages
# ✅ Prevent deletion if either server_id OR device_id is not null
# ✅ Use HTTP 409 Conflict status code for assignment conflicts
# ✅ Maintain referential integrity and business rules
#
# TEST SCENARIOS:
# ⏳ Delete available IP (should succeed)
# ⏳ Delete IP assigned to server only (should fail)
# ⏳ Delete IP assigned to device only (should fail)
# ⏳ Delete IP assigned to both server and device (should fail)
# ⏳ Delete non-existent IP (should return 404)
# ⏳ Verify error message contains entity names
#
# ========================================
